krizsan wrote:
> Hi,
> I'm a new debian-alpha user.
> We (the Department of Information Scienece) have a DS20 Alphaserver, we
> nedd tomcat, and struts.
> I tried to install tomcat with apt-get, and it installed it, but it
> didn't start.
> I tried to compile some source - failed.
> I tried to build from description :
> http://lists.debian.org/debian-alpha/2005/03/msg00057.html
> FAILED
> 
> Anybody write me the correct description of install tomcat4.
> PLEASE please ...

For tomcat on alpha either try SableVM, or CacaoJVM[1], or gij. As a
Kaffe dev, I know that Kaffe is currently very fragile on alpha[3] :( If
you run into bugs with SableVM or gij, please file bugs in the BTS. I'd
suggest trying out cacao, as the cacao devs are actively hacking on a
nice, fast jit for alpha, afaict.[2]

If you need help setting up cacao on an alpha, please join the IRC
channel #cacao on irc.freenode.net, twisti, one of the Cacao developers,
has a tomcat instance running on an alpha under cacao.

cheers,
dalibor topic

[1] www.cacaojvm.org
[2] And they could use users, being a really nice & helpful bunch. :)
[3] If you are interested in helping out with making kaffe run nice on
alpha hop on the kaffe mailing list, kaffe@kaffe.org.



