On a related note to proc problems.  The kernel wchan entries do not seem t=
o=20
be valid on either 2.6.10 or 2.6.12 (I haven't checked other versions).

When a process is suspended in the kernel, they should point to the functio=
n. =20
The /proc/xxxx/wchan should be a decoded version (i.e., looked up in=20
kallsyms), and the seventh entry from the end in /proc/xxxx/stat should be =
a=20
non-decoded version (i.e., the raw address).

On the Alpha, both entries are the same (i.e, raw address), and both seem t=
o=20
be garbage (i.e., the addresses do not even come anywhere close to actual=20
functions in /proc/kallsyms).

=2DT

=2D-=20
