>    For example I tried with dpkg -i php or dpkg -i php.deb etc.

dpkg is the command line tool for installing a package you made or =20
previously downloaded by yourself.

apt is the tool for automatically download and install a package and =20
its dependencies. dselect is an universal char-based front-end to apt.

try this, as root:

apt-get update
apt-get install php4

then give a look at dselect and what it could do for you.

bye!
gl :)


